      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108555",
      ":question/problem": "In a factory, two types of machines, type $A$ and type $B$, produce the same product. The random variable $X$ represents the number of rejects per day of a typical type $A$ machine. The random\nvariable $Y$ is the number of rejects per day of a typical type $B$ machine. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n| $x$$0$$1$$2$$3$$f(x)$$0.1$$0.6$$0.2$$0.1$ |  | $y$$0$$1$$2$$f(y)$$0.5$$0.3$$0.2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nIf the factory has $5$ type $A$ and $3$ type $B$ machines, calculate the expected number of items per day that the factory rejects.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
