      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-127990",
      ":question/problem": "The random variable $X$ represents the age of a randomly selected child from a football team, and the random variable $Y$  represents the age of a randomly selected child from a baseball team. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nOne child is selected at random from each team. Calculate the expected sum of ages of the two children."
    }
